From 6f6acc3b5e686fa2fd12c4b12f4130cddc2c1c6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: codezhzh123 <codezhzh123@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:10:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add opt-in SM2/SM3/SM4 support

Add ShangMi (GM/T) algorithm support:
- sm2-sm3 key exchange using the SM2 KAP and SM3;
- sm2 and sm2-cert key types (ssh-sm2), including PEM import/export;
- hmac-sm3 MAC and sm4-ctr cipher.

SM2 signing/verification computes Z per GM/T 0003.2 and emits a DER
ECDSA-Sig-Value.  OpenSSL 3 provider-backed SM2 keys are converted to
legacy EC_KEY for internal use.

The SM2 KAP user ID is derived with SM3("SM2-KAP-UID" || ...):
- initial KEX: client/server version strings and KEXINIT payloads;
- rekey: the SSH session ID.
This replaces the hardcoded 16-byte ID from the original openEuler 9.6
patch and therefore breaks SM2 KAP interoperability with it.  The KDF
checks for counter overflow, and the shared-secret buffer is cleared
before release.

The new algorithms are not added to the default proposals; they must be
enabled explicitly.  Build wiring, key handling, regression tests and
fuzz coverage are updated.  Non-OpenSSL builds keep a placeholder SM3
digest entry so digest lookup fails safely.

Signed-off-by: codezhzh123 <codezhzh123@outlook.com>
